course: dictionary
lesson: 4199
title: Goosebumps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Goosebumps are tiny bumps that come up on your skin. You get them when you are cold, scared or very excited. The word is often used in the plural, so say goosebumps. Look at the words around it to work out what it means.
explain: «Tiny muscles at the hair roots tighten, as when you get goosebumps.» Here goosebumps is a physical thing that happens to your skin. Now look at a different use: «Something that gives you goosebumps» means something that makes you feel thrilled, scared or deeply moved, even if your skin stays smooth.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The scary film gave me goosebumps» makes sense if goosebumps means feeling scared or thrilled. It does not mean you have a rash or a bug bite.
fact: Goosebumps are tiny bumps that appear on your skin.
fact: You get goosebumps when you are cold, scared or very excited.
fact: Goosebumps happen when tiny muscles at the bottom of each hair pull the hair upright.
fact: Goosebumps are also called goose pimples or goose flesh.
fact: In furry animals, goosebumps fluff up the fur to trap warm air or make the animal look bigger.
exercise: «Goosebumps are left from ancestors with fur: tiny muscles fluffed the fur up to keep warm or look bigger.» What are goosebumps? | Big bruises from a bump or fall | *Tiny bumps on your skin when you are cold, scared or excited | A kind of bird that lives on farms | Hairs that fall out in winter
exercise: «A frightened cat arches its back, stands sideways and fluffs out its fur to look bigger.» Why does the cat fluff out its fur? | To cool down in the sun | To go to sleep | To wash itself clean | *To look bigger
exercise: Ella says, «The scary film gave me goosebumps.» What does gave me goosebumps mean? | I got a bug bite on my arm | I need to see a doctor | *It made me feel thrilled, scared or deeply moved | I have a cold and a fever
test: «Your skin is your biggest organ, a living coat that keeps germs out, grows goosebumps in the cold.» What makes goosebumps appear? | *Being cold | Eating too much sugar | Reading a book | Going to bed late
test: Which words are other names for goosebumps? | Goose steps and goose honks | *Goose pimples and goose flesh | Goose eggs and goose feathers | Goose fat and goose meat
exam: Jayden reads, «Goosebumps happen when tiny muscles pull hairs upright.» What does this tell us about goosebumps? | They are big lumps under the skin caused by a bump | *They are tiny bumps on skin caused by tiny muscles pulling hairs upright | They only happen to animals with fur | They are a kind of hair that never moves
